course: dictionary
lesson: 15771
title: Short forms of days
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A short form is a shorter way of writing a word. Tues is a short form of Tuesday. You will see it where space is short, such as on timetables and calendars: «Mon, Tues, Wed».
explain: Tues can also be written as Tue or Tu. All three mean Tuesday, the day after Monday and before Wednesday.
explain: Short forms are useful in maths too. A problem might say, «Tues is the second day of the school week.» Which day comes after Monday? Tuesday, so Tues stands for Tuesday.
fact: Tues is an abbreviation, a short written form of Tuesday.
fact: Tuesday is the day after Monday and before Wednesday.
fact: You will see Tues on timetables, calendars, shop signs, diaries and notes, where space is short.
fact: Tue and Tu are other short forms that also mean Tuesday.
fact: In maths, Tues stands for Tuesday, the second day of the school week.
exercise: «Swimming club is on Tues at five o'clock.» What does Tues mean? | Tea time | *Tuesday | Tomorrow | Thursday
exercise: Look at the timetable: «Mon: maths. Tues: art. Wed: PE.» On which day is art? | Monday | Wednesday | Friday | *Tuesday
exercise: Which day comes right after Monday? Write the short form. | Wed | *Tues | Fri | Sun
test: «Mon, Tues, Wed» are shown on a calendar. Which day is Tues short for? | Monday | *Tuesday | Wednesday | Thursday
test: Maya writes «Tue» in her diary. What does she mean? | *Tuesday | Monday | Wednesday
exam: Ben's note says, «Meet you at the park on Tues.» Which day is he meeting Maya? | Saturday | *Tuesday | Thursday | Sunday
